+# ADR-0017: ERP port operation `readAdvisor`
+
+- **Status:** Accepted
+- **Date:** 2026-11-04
+- **Deciders:** lab-approver (accepted with the AN-902 spec, 2026-11-04)
+- **Sources:** T3-D-005, T3-AC-001, T2-D-009, AN-902, [ERP conventions](../conventions/erp.md)
+
+## Context
+
+Head office needs advisor master data. The ERP runs it (discovery baseline, "The ERP runs"). Every module reaches the ERP only through the `integration` module and its port (T3-D-005, T3-AC-001); the port has one operation per ERP read and a Zod schema per payload. The port has only `readCustomer` today. Every read records its source version and read time (T2-D-009). The NAV adapter, and later the Business Central adapter, must implement every port operation, so a new operation is a contract change.
+
+## Options
+
+1. **A new operation `readAdvisor(advisorNumber)` with the payload `AdvisorMasterData`.** Good: one operation per ERP read, as the port rules say; adapters implement it on their own. Bad: one more operation for every adapter.
+2. **A generic `readMasterData(kind, key)`.** Good: fewer methods. Bad: a weak contract, the payload type depends on a string; against the port rule "one method per operation".
+3. **Read advisor data from a copy table in `erp_copy`.** Good: works when the ERP is down. Bad: needs a refresh flow and a table; not needed for one head office read.
+
+## Decision
+
+We choose option 1. `ErpPort.readAdvisor(advisorNumber: string): Promise<AdvisorMasterData | null>`, `null` when the ERP has no such advisor. `AdvisorMasterData` has `advisorNumber` (`B` + 5 digits), `givenName`, `familyName`, `email`, `active` (boolean) and `sourceVersion`. `integration` exposes it as `readAdvisor`, returning `ErpRead<AdvisorMasterData>`; `identity` exposes `getAdvisor`. A copy table can follow when a flow needs it.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Head office and later the advisor portal read advisor master data through one typed contract.
+- The NAV adapter must implement `readAdvisor` and map the NAV fields; the mapping is open until the adapter exists.
+- A read fails with `ErpUnavailableError` when the ERP is down; the caller decides the fallback.
+- `pnpm arch` keeps the port inside `integration`; the type checker makes every adapter implement the operation.
